{"result": "{\n    \"title\": \"Nutritional Support Community: Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community focuses on nutritional support methods, particularly enteral and parenteral nutrition, which are essential for patients unable to consume food orally. Key entities include various nutritional methods, formulas, and medical conditions that necessitate these interventions, highlighting their interconnections and significance in patient care.\",\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the critical role of nutritional support in managing severe health conditions and improving patient outcomes.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Importance of Enteral Nutrition\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Enteral nutrition is a vital method for delivering nutrients directly to patients who cannot consume food orally. It is particularly beneficial for critically ill patients, those with swallowing difficulties, and individuals with chronic illnesses. Enteral nutrition helps maintain the integrity of the intestinal barrier, reduces infection risks, and improves overall nutritional status. This method is preferred over parenteral nutrition when the digestive tract is functional, as it has lower complication rates and better outcomes in critically ill patients [Data: Entities (347); Relationships (2599, 269, 2640)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Parenteral Nutrition\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Parenteral nutrition is utilized when enteral nutrition is not feasible, providing essential nutrients intravenously. It is crucial for patients with conditions that impair their ability to utilize the digestive tract effectively, such as severe pancreatitis or intestinal obstructions. While parenteral nutrition is necessary in certain cases, it is associated with higher complication rates compared to enteral nutrition, making the choice between the two methods critical based on patient conditions [Data: Entities (2599); Relationships (2599, 4639)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Clinical Guidelines and Recommendations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Organizations like the European Association of Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition (ESPEN) and the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) provide essential guidelines for the use of enteral and parenteral nutrition. These guidelines help healthcare professionals determine the appropriate nutritional support for patients based on their specific medical conditions, ensuring that nutritional interventions are tailored to individual needs [Data: Entities (13681, 2731); Relationships (4811, 264)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Nutritional Formulas and Their Applications\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Various specialized nutritional formulas are designed to meet the unique dietary needs of patients with specific health conditions. These formulas, including polymeric, oligomeric, and elemental types, are crucial for patients with digestive issues, metabolic disorders, or those recovering from surgery. The choice of formula can significantly influence patient recovery and overall health outcomes [Data: Entities (4876, 4873); Relationships (2659, 2660)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Impact of Medical Conditions on Nutritional Needs\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Certain medical conditions, such as acute renal failure, cancer, and Crohn's disease, necessitate specific nutritional interventions. Enteral nutrition is often employed to stabilize the nutritional status of patients with these conditions, ensuring they receive adequate nutrients to support their recovery. Understanding the interplay between these conditions and nutritional support is essential for effective patient management [Data: Entities (10081, 1472); Relationships (899, 2775)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Complications Associated with Nutritional Support\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While enteral and parenteral nutrition are critical for patient care, they can also lead to complications. Enteral nutrition may cause digestive symptoms or infections, while parenteral nutrition is associated with risks such as aluminum toxicity and metabolic imbalances. Careful management and monitoring are necessary to mitigate these risks and ensure patient safety [Data: Entities (11473, 4848); Relationships (4873, 2809)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"The Role of Age in Nutritional Support\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Age significantly influences the nutritional needs and interventions for patients. Elderly patients often require tailored nutritional support due to age-related health considerations, making it essential to adjust enteral nutrition strategies accordingly. This demographic factor is crucial in determining the type and amount of nutritional support provided [Data: Entities (2535, 2888); Relationships (2889, 2535)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Research Contributions to Nutritional Practices\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Researchers like De Luis Román DA and studies such as those by Kim et al. have significantly contributed to the understanding of enteral and parenteral nutrition. Their work informs best practices and guidelines, enhancing the quality of care provided to patients requiring nutritional support. Ongoing research is vital for advancing nutritional therapies and improving patient outcomes [Data: Entities (4848, 13368); Relationships (4737, 4804)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n347,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a vital method of delivering nutrition directly to the gastrointestinal tract, primarily designed for patients who are unable to consume food orally. This approach is often favored over parenteral nutrition due to its physiological benefits, safety, and efficacy. It involves administering nutrients either orally or through a feeding tube directly into the stomach or intestines, making it suitable for a variety of patient populations, including those with swallowing difficulties, chronic illnesses, or post-surgical needs.\n\nThis method is particularly beneficial for critically ill patients, individuals with severe dysphagia, and those with conditions that impair nutrient absorption, such as cystic fibrosis or pancreatitis. It is also extensively utilized in pediatric care, especially for premature infants, to ensure adequate growth and development. NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL helps maintain the integrity of the intestinal barrier, reduces the risk of infections, and improves overall nutritional status.\n\nIn clinical settings, enteral nutrition is typically initiated when oral intake is insufficient, often starting 5-7 days before surgery and continuing postoperatively. It is tailored to meet individual caloric and nutritional needs, utilizing specially formulated diets. However, it may present complications, such as digestive symptoms or increased infection risk, necessitating careful management to avoid interactions with medications.\n\nNUTRICIÓN ENTERAL serves as a critical intervention for patients who cannot meet their nutritional requirements through traditional means, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients to support their health and recovery. It is particularly indicated for patients with conditions like neoplasia, fistulas, and Crohn's disease, and is essential for maintaining digestive tract integrity and minimizing inflammatory responses. Overall, this nutritional support method has developed significantly in recent years and is preferred when the digestive tract is functional, making it a cornerstone of modern nutritional therapy.\",335\r\n6841,APACHE II,\"APACHE II is a severity scoring system designed to evaluate the prognosis of critically ill patients, including those suffering from acute pancreatitis. This scoring system measures the severity of illness in patients, providing a quantitative assessment that helps in determining the risk of complications. Specifically, a score of 10 or higher on the APACHE II scale indicates an increased risk of adverse outcomes. The tool is widely utilized in clinical settings to guide treatment decisions and improve patient management for those in critical condition.\",3\r\n14461,FÓRMULA,\"FÓRMULA es un sustituto de la leche materna utilizado para alimentar a los recién nacidos, especialmente aquellos que son prematuros. Esta fórmula está diseñada para satisfacer las necesidades nutricionales específicas de estos infantes. Además, las fórmulas de nutrición enteral son preparaciones que proporcionan nutrientes a pacientes que no pueden alimentarse por vía oral, lo que resalta la versatilidad y la importancia de las fórmulas en el ámbito de la nutrición médica y pediátrica.\",2\r\n7171,SONDA DE GASTROYEYUNOSTOMÍA,\"The \"\"SONDA DE GASTROYEYUNOSTOMÍA\"\" is a medical device specifically designed for the administration of enteral nutrition. It is utilized in the treatment of patients who require long-term nutritional support. This device plays a crucial role in ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients when they are unable to consume food orally.\",2\r\n11473,ALUMINIO,\"Aluminio is a chemical element that serves as a component in certain antacids. It has been noted for its ability to inhibit gastric motility, which can lead to gastrointestinal complications, particularly when combined with enteral nutrition. Additionally, aluminum is associated with toxicity in parenteral nutrition, which can adversely affect bone mass. The element is linked to various medical conditions and poses a risk of intoxication, highlighting the need for caution in its use within medical treatments.\",3\r\n4848,DE LUIS ROMÁN DA,\"De Luis Román DA is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of nutrition, specifically in the areas of enteral and parenteral nutrition. He has been referenced in discussions regarding the administration methods of enteral nutrition, highlighting his expertise in this area. Additionally, De Luis Román DA has addressed the complications associated with parenteral nutrition, further demonstrating his comprehensive understanding of nutritional practices. His work has significantly contributed to the literature on enteral nutrition, establishing him as a notable figure in this domain.\",3\r\n13681,ASOCIACIÓN EUROPEA DE NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL,The European Association of Enteral and Parenteral Nutrition (ESPEN) recommends preoperative enteral nutrition for patients undergoing major abdominal surgery.,2\r\n13059,FALLO RESPIRATORIO AGUDO,,2\r\n11131,FÍSTULAS DEL CONDUCTO TORÁCICO,\"Las fístulas del conducto torácico son condiciones médicas que pueden requerir tratamiento nutricional especializado, como la nutrición enteral o parenteral.\",2\r\n13368,KIM ET AL.,Kim et al. son investigadores que realizaron un estudio sobre la comparación de la nutrición enteral y parenteral en pacientes gastrectomizados.,2\r\n1867,OBSTRUCCIÓN INTESTINAL,\"\"\"OBSTRUCCIÓN INTESTINAL\"\" refers to a medical condition characterized by a blockage that prevents food or liquid from passing through the small or large intestine. This blockage complicates nutritional treatment and can hinder normal food intake, often necessitating enteral nutrition. However, in some cases, intestinal obstruction may contraindicate enteral nutrition, requiring alternative approaches such as parenteral nutrition. This condition is particularly relevant in patients with cancer, as it can significantly impede their ability to consume adequate food. Intestinal obstruction is noted to be the second most frequent indication for nutritional support, accounting for 25.6% of cases.\",2\r\n4876,FÓRMULAS ESPECÍFICAS,\"Fórmulas específicas are specialized nutritional formulas tailored for patients with specific health conditions, including diabetes and various metabolic or digestive diseases. These formulas serve as nutritional solutions that are adapted to meet the unique needs of individuals suffering from these conditions. They are designed not only to provide essential nutrients but also to influence the evolution and prognosis of certain diseases, thereby supporting the overall health and well-being of patients.\",4\r\n2482,ALIMENTACIÓN ORAL,\"Alimentación oral refers to the process of consuming food by mouth. This method may be transitioned to after enteral nutrition in stable patients. It is particularly significant in the management of patients with intestinal failure, as it plays a crucial role in their nutritional care. However, the ability to engage in alimentación oral can be affected in patients experiencing malnutrition or gastrointestinal issues. Therefore, the safety of oral feeding is often evaluated in patients who have been receiving enteral nutrition to ensure that they can safely consume food through the mouth.\",3\r\n2535,EDAD,\"EDAD, which stands for \"\"Elderly Demographic Age Data,\"\" plays a crucial role in understanding age-related health considerations. It provides recommendations for catheter sizes and fluid intake tailored to the needs of older patients. Furthermore, EDAD is identified as a significant predictor of the necessity for enteral nutrition, especially in individuals aged 80 years and older. This highlights the importance of age in influencing surgical outcomes and underscores the need for age-specific medical strategies.\",3\r\n10081,FALLO RENAL AGUDO,\"FALLO RENAL AGUDO, or acute renal failure, is characterized by a sudden loss of kidney function. This condition necessitates nutritional support and careful monitoring of electrolytes to manage the patient's health effectively.\",3\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n2600,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,PACIENTE,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a medical procedure utilized to provide nutritional support to patients who are unable to consume food orally. This method is particularly important for patients like the PACIENTE, who may have specific medical conditions that necessitate enteral nutrition to ensure adequate nutrient intake. The PACIENTE is the recipient of this nutrition, which is tailored to meet their individual nutritional needs, influenced by their medical condition.\n\nIn cases where the PACIENTE has moderate malnutrition or conditions such as renal failure or dysphagia, enteral nutrition becomes essential. It is administered through various means, including gastrostomy and nasogastric tubes, to facilitate recovery and improve the patient's nutritional status. The decision to initiate enteral nutrition is often made when the PACIENTE is unable to meet their dietary requirements through oral intake, as seen in situations where they cannot feed themselves or have ineffective oral intake.\n\nWhile enteral nutrition is beneficial, it can also lead to complications such as diarrhea, which may arise from factors related to the method of administration or the specific nutritional products used. Overall, enteral nutrition plays a critical role in the management of the PACIENTE's health, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients for recovery and overall well-being.\",881\r\n2599,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL are two distinct methods of providing nutritional support to patients who are unable to consume food orally or utilize their digestive tract effectively. Both approaches are essential for patients with various medical conditions, including those with respiratory issues and those who have undergone gastrectomy. \n\nNUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is generally preferred over NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL due to its lower complication rates, reduced costs, and better outcomes in critically ill patients. It is particularly favored when the digestive tract is functional, such as in cases of severe pancreatitis, where enteral nutrition is the first choice. However, NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL is indicated when enteral nutrition is not tolerated or when the digestive system cannot be used adequately. \n\nBoth methods can be utilized in pediatric care and may be employed in conjunction when enteral nutrition alone is insufficient. Nutritional support can transition from parenteral to enteral as patients adapt and their conditions improve. Overall, the choice between NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL depends on the specific needs and conditions of the patient, with a general preference for enteral methods when feasible.\",773\r\n445,PACIENTES,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,\"Enteral nutrition is a critical medical intervention utilized for patients who are unable to consume food orally due to various health conditions. This form of nutrition is particularly essential for patients undergoing procedures such as esophagectomy, as it supports their recovery process. Additionally, patients suffering from severe dysphagia are often recommended to receive enteral nutrition through a feeding tube to ensure they receive adequate nutrition and maintain their digestive health. Overall, patients are the primary recipients of enteral nutrition, which is designed to meet their specific dietary needs when oral intake is not feasible.\",562\r\n3268,PACIENTE,APACHE II,El paciente tiene una puntuación en el índice APACHE II que indica la gravedad de su condición,549\r\n3489,PACIENTE,FÓRMULA,La fórmula de nutrición enteral se elige en función de las características y necesidades del paciente.,548\r\n3414,PACIENTE,SONDA DE GASTROYEYUNOSTOMÍA,Se colocó una sonda de gastroyeyunostomía en el paciente como parte de su tratamiento.,548\r\n4873,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,ALUMINIO,\"Aluminum toxicity is a concern in parenteral nutrition, impacting patient outcomes\",441\r\n4737,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,DE LUIS ROMÁN DA,De Luis Román DA is an author who contributed to the literature on parenteral nutrition,441\r\n4811,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,ASOCIACIÓN EUROPEA DE NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL,ESPEN provides guidelines on the use of parenteral nutrition for patients who cannot receive enteral nutrition.,440\r\n4794,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,FALLO RESPIRATORIO AGUDO,Fallo Respiratorio Agudo often necessitates the use of parenteral nutrition when enteral routes are not viable,440\r\n4760,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,FÍSTULAS DEL CONDUCTO TORÁCICO,Las fístulas del conducto torácico pueden requerir nutrición parenteral en casos donde la nutrición enteral no es suficiente,440\r\n4804,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,KIM ET AL.,Kim et al. también compararon la nutrición parenteral en su estudio sobre pacientes gastrectomizados.,440\r\n4639,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,OBSTRUCCIÓN INTESTINAL,\"La obstrucción intestinal puede contraindicar la nutrición enteral, requiriendo nutrición parenteral\",440\r\n2690,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,MALNUTRICIÓN,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a medical intervention that is frequently employed to address MALNUTRICIÓN, particularly in patients who are unable to consume food orally. This form of nutrition is especially recommended for patients experiencing malnutrition who are undergoing surgical procedures. By providing essential nutrients directly into the gastrointestinal tract, enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in the management and treatment of malnutrition in various clinical settings.\",439\r\n2602,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and NUTRICIÓN ARTIFICIAL refer to forms of nutritional support provided to patients who are unable to consume food orally. Enteral nutrition is a specific type of artificial nutrition that is particularly recommended for patients experiencing moderate to severe health issues, including those with diabetes. It is utilized when patients cannot feed themselves through traditional oral means, ensuring they receive essential nutrients. \n\nIn clinical settings, enteral nutrition is a common practice and is often employed as part of a broader nutritional intervention strategy. While enteral feeding is a primary method of providing nutritional support, it may not always be sufficient on its own, indicating that additional nutritional support methods may be necessary. Overall, enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in the management of patients requiring artificial nutrition, ensuring they receive adequate dietary intake when oral consumption is not feasible.\",428\r\n2644,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ESPEN,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a key focus of the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN), which provides guidelines and recommendations for its use in various clinical scenarios. According to ESPEN, enteral nutrition is particularly beneficial for patients with liver diseases, as it can help manage their nutritional needs effectively. Additionally, ESPEN advocates for enteral nutrition as a method to enhance intestinal adaptation, which is crucial for patients recovering from gastrointestinal surgeries or conditions. Furthermore, ESPEN emphasizes the importance of enteral nutrition for critically ill patients, highlighting its role in supporting their overall health and recovery during critical care.\",420\r\n942,DESNUTRICIÓN,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,La desnutrición puede ser una razón para iniciar la nutrición enteral en pacientes pediátricos.,409\r\n2774,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,CÁNCER,La nutrición enteral se utiliza para estabilizar el estado nutricional de pacientes con cáncer que no pueden ingerir alimentos por vía oral,401\r\n2608,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,PROTEÍNAS,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and PROTEÍNAS are closely related in the context of nutritional support for patients, particularly those with metabolic disorders. Proteins are an essential component of enteral nutrition, playing a crucial role in maintaining glucose levels in these patients. Nutritional support through enteral feeding prominently includes proteins as a key element, highlighting their importance in ensuring adequate nutrition and metabolic stability.\",392\r\n2738,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA INTESTINAL,\"La nutrición enteral es un método de tratamiento utilizado para pacientes con enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal. Este enfoque puede mejorar la situación intestinal y facilitar la recuperación de estos pacientes. Además, la nutrición enteral es especialmente importante en casos de enfermedad inflamatoria intestinal grave, ya que asegura una nutrición adecuada, lo que es crucial para el manejo de la condición.\",392\r\n2641,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,PANCREATITIS AGUDA,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and PANCREATITIS AGUDA are closely related in the context of managing patients with acute pancreatitis. Acute pancreatitis can complicate the administration of enteral nutrition due to the reduced stimulation of pancreatic secretions. However, enteral nutrition is considered essential when patients with acute pancreatitis are stable enough to tolerate oral intake. It plays a crucial role in the management of these patients, particularly in severe cases, as it ensures adequate nutritional support and helps reduce the incidence of infections, thereby improving recovery outcomes.\n\nEnteral nutrition is recommended for patients with acute pancreatitis to enhance their nutritional status and support clinical evolution. It serves as a vital nutritional intervention through the gastrointestinal tract, which is beneficial for patients suffering from this condition. Overall, enteral nutrition is recognized as a key treatment option for managing acute pancreatitis, especially in more severe forms of the disease, to ensure proper nourishment and facilitate recovery.\",389\r\n2643,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,CIRROSIS,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a form of nutritional support that may be necessary for patients with CIRROSIS who are unable to maintain adequate oral intake or meet their nutritional needs through oral means. This intervention is crucial for ensuring that individuals with CIRROSIS receive the essential nutrients required for their health and recovery, particularly when their ability to consume food normally is compromised.\",389\r\n2722,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,HIERRO,Iron supplementation may be necessary for patients receiving enteral nutrition and erythropoietin,380\r\n2610,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is essential for patients suffering from INSUFICIENCIA RENAL, particularly those experiencing acute renal failure who are unable to maintain adequate nutritional intake. Specialized nutritional formulas are specifically designed to manage the dietary needs of individuals with renal insufficiency, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients while considering their condition.\",376\r\n2710,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,CIRUGÍA BARIÁTRICA,La nutrición enteral puede ser utilizada en el seguimiento postoperatorio de pacientes que se han sometido a cirugía bariátrica,376\r\n2731,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ASPEN,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a field that is significantly influenced by the guidelines developed by ASPEN (the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition). ASPEN creates comprehensive guidelines for enteral nutrition that are applicable to both adult and pediatric patients. These guidelines include specific recommendations for the use of enteral nutrition in various clinical scenarios, such as in patients with pancreatitis and those requiring nutritional support following surgery. Additionally, ASPEN emphasizes the importance of specialized nutritional support for patients who need enteral nutrition, ensuring that their unique needs are met effectively.\",376\r\n2701,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO 2,La diabetes mellitus tipo 2 requiere un ajuste cuidadoso de la nutrición enteral para controlar los niveles de glucosa en sangre,375\r\n2619,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,GLUTAMINA,Glutamine is included in enteral diets to support gut health,369\r\n2719,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,VITAMINA C,Vitamin C levels must be monitored in patients receiving enteral nutrition to avoid toxicity,369\r\n2680,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a critical intervention for patients diagnosed with SÍNDROME DE INTESTINO CORTO, commonly known as short bowel syndrome. This condition arises when a significant portion of the small intestine is absent or has been surgically removed, leading to challenges in nutrient absorption. To address these challenges, enteral nutrition is employed to ensure that patients receive an adequate intake of essential nutrients despite the reduced length of their intestines. Consequently, patients with short bowel syndrome often rely on enteral nutrition support to meet their dietary needs and maintain their overall health.\",368\r\n2728,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,QUILOTÓRAX,La nutrición enteral se recomienda como tratamiento para pacientes con quilotórax que no pueden alimentarse por vía oral,368\r\n2638,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CRÓNICA,Nutritional support through enteral nutrition is indicated for patients with chronic kidney disease who cannot be nourished orally.,365\r\n2780,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ALBUMINA,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and ALBUMINA are interconnected in the context of patient care, particularly in post-surgical settings. Albúmina levels play a significant role in influencing the binding of drugs in the plasma, which is crucial when considering enteral nutrition. Furthermore, early enteral nutrition has been associated with increases in albúmina levels in post-surgical patients, highlighting the importance of timely nutritional intervention in enhancing protein levels and potentially improving drug efficacy.\",365\r\n2793,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,TRASPLANTE DE CÉLULAS HEMATOLÓGICAS,La nutrición enteral puede ser necesaria para pacientes que no pueden satisfacer sus necesidades nutricionales durante el trasplante,365\r\n2716,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is an essential component in the management of patients suffering from INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA. It is particularly recommended for those individuals who are unable to adequately consume food orally. Enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in supporting the nutritional needs of these patients, ensuring they receive the necessary nutrients during their treatment for acute renal failure.\",363\r\n2718,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,VITAMINA A,Vitamin A levels need to be monitored in patients receiving enteral nutrition to prevent overdose,361\r\n2849,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,VARÓN,El varón de 75 años está recibiendo nutrición enteral debido a su incapacidad para alimentarse por vía oral.,360\r\n2850,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,IMC,La nutrición enteral se evalúa en función del IMC del paciente para determinar su estado nutricional.,358\r\n899,QUIMIOTERAPIA,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,La quimioterapia puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrición enteral debido a la incapacidad de los pacientes para alimentarse adecuadamente.,358\r\n2658,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,TABLA 1,\"La Tabla 1 proporciona información sobre las indicaciones clínicas de la nutrición enteral, lo que es relevante para su aplicación en pediatría.\",357\r\n2775,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,CÁNCER GÁSTRICO,\"La nutrición enteral se utiliza para mejorar el estado nutricional de los pacientes con cáncer gástrico que no pueden alimentarse por vía oral. Además, es un tratamiento importante para aquellos pacientes que han sido sometidos a cirugía debido a esta enfermedad, ya que contribuye a mejorar su recuperación.\",357\r\n2651,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,TRASPLANTE HEPÁTICO,\"Nutritional support, including enteral nutrition, is critical for patients undergoing liver transplantation\",355\r\n2698,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,UCI,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL es un enfoque terapéutico que se utiliza frecuentemente en la UCI (Unidad de Cuidados Intensivos) para mejorar el estado nutricional de los pacientes críticos. Este tipo de nutrición puede ser especialmente beneficioso para aquellos pacientes que padecen condiciones graves, como la pancreatitis, ya que su administración puede contribuir a una mejor evolución clínica. Además, se ha observado que la nutrición enteral puede reducir la duración de la estancia en la UCI, lo que resalta su importancia en el manejo de pacientes en estado crítico.\",355\r\n1472,ENFERMEDAD DE CROHN,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,Nutritional support through enteral nutrition is used as a primary treatment for Crohn's disease to prevent malnutrition and induce remission,354\r\n2756,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SÍNDROME DE REALIMENTACIÓN,La nutrición enteral puede provocar el síndrome de realimentación si no se monitoriza adecuadamente la reintroducción de la alimentación.,351\r\n2888,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,PACIENTE PEDIÁTRICO,Los pacientes pediátricos a menudo requieren nutrición enteral debido a sus necesidades específicas de desarrollo y salud.,348\r\n2884,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,RECIÉN NACIDOS PREMATUROS,\"La nutrición enteral es esencial para el cuidado y la alimentación de los recién nacidos prematuros, ayudando a evitar complicaciones como la desnutrición.\",346\r\n2087,PACIENTES GERIÁTRICOS,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,La nutrición enteral es especialmente indicada para pacientes geriátricos que tienen dificultades para la ingesta oral,346\r\n2625,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SONDA ENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition to patients who are unable to consume food orally. This is accomplished through the use of a SONDA ENTERAL, which is a feeding tube specifically designed for this purpose. The SONDA ENTERAL serves as the means by which nutrición enteral is administered, ensuring that patients receive the necessary nutrients directly into their digestive system.\",345\r\n2627,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SNG,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL refers to the provision of nutrition through the gastrointestinal tract, typically in patients who are unable to consume food orally. The SNG, or sonda nasogástrica, is a medical device specifically designed for this purpose. It is utilized to administer enteral nutrition to patients who cannot initiate oral intake or who are unable to feed themselves through normal means. The SNG is commonly employed in clinical settings to ensure that patients receive the necessary nutrients when oral feeding is not feasible.\",345\r\n2659,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FÓRMULAS POLIMÉRICAS,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL se refiere a la administración de nutrientes directamente en el tracto gastrointestinal, y dentro de este contexto, las FÓRMULAS POLIMÉRICAS son un tipo específico de preparación utilizada. Estas fórmulas están diseñadas para pacientes que tienen una función gastrointestinal adecuada, lo que significa que pueden absorber y digerir los nutrientes sin problemas. En resumen, las fórmulas poliméricas son productos utilizados en la nutrición enteral, especialmente indicadas para aquellos pacientes que no presentan dificultades en la absorción o digestión de los alimentos.\",345\r\n2746,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SONDA NASOENTERAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL refers to the method of providing nutrition directly to the gastrointestinal tract, typically through a tube, for patients who are unable to consume food orally. The SONDA NASOENTERAL, or nasoenteric tube, is specifically designed for this purpose. It is utilized to administer enteral nutrition to patients who cannot feed themselves through traditional means. Both descriptions emphasize the role of the nasoenteric tube in facilitating enteral nutrition for individuals with feeding difficulties.\",345\r\n2747,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,GASTROSTOMÍA QUIRÚRGICA,GASTROSTOMÍA QUIRÚRGICA is a method for providing NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,344\r\n2772,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,TUMORES DE CABEZA Y CUELLO,Enteral nutrition may be required for patients with head and neck tumors who cannot eat normally,344\r\n2906,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,NUTRICIÓN ORAL,La nutrición enteral se utiliza cuando la nutrición oral no es suficiente para satisfacer las necesidades del paciente.,344\r\n2637,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FRA,Enteral nutrition is often utilized for patients with acute renal failure who cannot meet their nutritional needs orally.,343\r\n2706,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SONDA DE GASTROSTOMÍA,\"La sonda de gastrostomía es otra opción para la nutrición enteral del paciente, utilizada cuando la sonda de gastroyeyunostomía no es efectiva\",343\r\n2640,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,DIÁLISIS PERITONEAL,Patients undergoing peritoneal dialysis may also need enteral nutrition for adequate nutrient intake.,341\r\n2647,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,SONDA NASOYEYUNAL,Nasojejunal tubes are used for enteral nutrition when gastric feeding is not possible,341\r\n2686,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FÓRMULAS OLIGOMONOMÉRICAS,Las fórmulas oligomonoméricas son un tipo de producto utilizado en la nutrición enteral,341\r\n2735,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,INFECCIONES,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL es un enfoque nutricional que se ha demostrado eficaz en la reducción del riesgo de infecciones en diversos contextos clínicos. En particular, se ha observado que la nutrición enteral precoz puede disminuir el riesgo de infecciones postquirúrgicas en pacientes con cáncer gástrico. Además, este tipo de nutrición también ha mostrado una reducción en la incidencia de infecciones en pacientes que sufren de pancreatitis aguda. Por lo tanto, la implementación de la nutrición enteral puede ser una estrategia valiosa para mejorar los resultados clínicos y minimizar el riesgo de infecciones en estos grupos de pacientes.\",341\r\n2611,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ENCEFALOPATÍA HEPÁTICA,Nutritional formulas are specifically designed for managing hepatic encephalopathy,340\r\n2614,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ACEITES VEGETALES,Vegetable oils are a component of enteral nutrition formulas,340\r\n2660,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FÓRMULAS OLIGOMÉRICAS,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL refers to a method of providing nutrition directly to the gastrointestinal tract, typically through a feeding tube. Within this context, FÓRMULAS OLIGOMÉRICAS, or oligomeric formulas, are specifically designed for patients who experience difficulties with digestion or absorption. These formulas are particularly beneficial for individuals with various digestive issues, as they are easier to digest and absorb compared to standard formulas. Overall, oligomeric formulas serve as a vital component of enteral nutrition, offering essential nutritional support to patients with compromised digestive function.\",340\r\n2703,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,PEG,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a method of providing essential nutrients directly to individuals who may have difficulty consuming food orally. This process is often implemented through the placement of a gastrostomía percutánea endoscópica (PEG), which is a technique that facilitates the delivery of nutrition directly into the stomach. The PEG procedure ensures that patients receive adequate nutrient intake, thereby supporting their overall health and well-being.\",340\r\n2806,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,METOCLOPRAMIDA,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL refers to the provision of nutrition through the gastrointestinal tract, typically used for patients who cannot consume food orally. METOCLOPRAMIDA, also known as metoclopramide, is a medication that aids in gastric emptying, which is crucial for patients receiving enteral nutrition. It enhances gastric emptying, thereby improving tolerance to enteral nutrition in these patients. This medication is particularly beneficial for individuals who may experience delayed gastric emptying, ensuring that they can better assimilate the nutrients provided through enteral feeding.\",340\r\n2862,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,OSTOMÍAS,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL and OSTOMÍAS are interconnected in the context of medical procedures for patients requiring long-term nutritional support. Ostomies are surgical interventions that may be performed on patients who need enteral nutrition, providing a means for these individuals to receive essential nutrients when traditional methods are not viable. This surgical option is particularly relevant for those who require ongoing enteral nutrition, highlighting the role of ostomies in facilitating adequate dietary intake for patients with specific health needs.\",340\r\n2685,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FÓRMULAS ESPECÍFICAS,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL encompasses various methods of providing nutrition directly to the gastrointestinal tract, and within this field, FÓRMULAS ESPECÍFICAS play a crucial role. These specific formulas are designed to meet the unique dietary needs of individuals with particular health conditions, ensuring that their nutritional requirements are adequately addressed. Thus, FÓRMULAS ESPECÍFICAS are a vital component of NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL, tailored to support the health and recovery of patients with specific medical needs.\",339\r\n2684,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FÓRMULAS ESTÁNDAR,Las fórmulas estándar son un tipo de fórmula utilizada en la nutrición enteral,339\r\n2704,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,DESNUTRICIÓN MODERADA,Enteral nutrition is being implemented to address the patient's moderate malnutrition,339\r\n2828,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ALIMENTACIÓN ORAL,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL y ALIMENTACIÓN ORAL son dos métodos de proporcionar nutrientes a los pacientes. La nutrición enteral se evalúa en comparación con la alimentación oral para determinar cuál es la mejor opción para cada paciente. Este tipo de nutrición se utiliza especialmente cuando la alimentación oral no es suficiente o no es posible debido a condiciones médicas. En resumen, la nutrición enteral es una alternativa crucial cuando la alimentación oral no puede satisfacer las necesidades nutricionales del paciente.\",338\r\n2809,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,ALUMINIO,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL refers to the process of providing nutrition to individuals who are unable to consume food orally, often through specialized formulas delivered via a feeding tube. ALUMINIO, commonly found in antacids, can have significant implications for enteral nutrition. Specifically, the presence of aluminio in antacids can inhibit gastric motility, which may adversely affect the absorption and effectiveness of enteral nutrition. Additionally, the use of aluminio in antiácidos can lead to gastrointestinal issues when combined with enteral nutrition. Therefore, caution is advised when using aluminum-containing antacids in patients receiving enteral nutrition, as it may disrupt their digestive processes and overall nutritional intake.\",338\r\n2696,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,APACHE II,Una puntuación mayor o igual a 10 en el índice APACHE II indica que los pacientes son candidatos para recibir nutrición enteral.,338\r\n2675,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,DE LUIS ROMÁN DA,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is a field of study that focuses on providing nutrition to individuals who cannot obtain adequate nutrition through oral intake. De Luis Román DA is an author who has made significant contributions to this area, enhancing the understanding and knowledge surrounding enteral nutrition. He has written extensively on the subject, sharing insights and research that inform best practices in the administration and management of enteral nutrition.\",338\r\n2889,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,EDAD,La edad del paciente influye en la cantidad y tipo de nutrición enteral que se debe administrar.,338\r\n2717,NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL,FALLO RENAL AGUDO,\"NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL is essential for patients suffering from FALLO RENAL AGUDO, particularly for those who are unable to maintain adequate dietary intake. Nutritional support through enteral nutrition plays a crucial role in the management of acut